      "title": "Human Argonaute 2 is a programmable targeting domain for RNA editing",
      "abstract": "Nature Biotechnology, Published online: 22 October 2026; doi:10.1038/s41587-026-03358-zALTER is a programmable RNA base editor built entirely from human proteins. By using human AGO2 instead of bacterial CRISPR–Cas proteins, ALTER mitigates a key risk factor for harmful immune responses in therapeutic applications while also proving generally more effective than dCas13-based editors.",
